  "final_answer": "I successfully navigated to the Cambridge Dictionary page for \"sustainability.\" Here are the findings:\n\n## Word: **sustainability**\n\n**Part of speech:** noun [U]\n\n### 🔊 Pronunciation\n- **UK (British English):** /səˌsteɪ.nəˈbɪl.ə.ti/\n- **US (American English):** /səˌsteɪ.nəˈbɪl.ə.t̬i/\n\n(The page also offers audio playback buttons for both British and American pronunciations.)\n\n### 📖 Definitions\n\n**1. General meaning:**\nThe quality of being able to continue over a period of time.\n- *Example:* \"the long-term sustainability of the community\"\n\n**2. Environment (C2 level):**\nThe quality of causing little or no damage to the environment and therefore able to continue for a long time.\n- *Example:* \"the company's commitment to environmental sustainability\"\n\n**3. Business English:**\nThe idea that goods and services should be produced in ways that do not use resources that cannot be replaced and that do not damage the environment.\n- *Example:* \"The successful coffee chain promotes sustainability with its use of recycled paper cups.\"\n\n*(Source: Cambridge Advanced Learner's Dictionary & Thesaurus © Cambridge University Press)*",
